INSERT INTO `quest_offer_reward` (`ID`, `Emote1`, `Emote2`, `Emote3`, `Emote4`, `EmoteDelay1`, `EmoteDelay2`, `EmoteDelay3`, `EmoteDelay4`, `RewardText`, `VerifiedBuild`) VALUES
(41686, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'External forces, I reckon? We\'re hard at work, so any new pair of hands is welcome.', 0),
(41692, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '<Your surroundings suggest a fierce battle has taken place here, the carrion birds lurking around the ruined camp paint a grim picture. The journal you find among the scattered supplies may hold a clue on what happened here.>', 0),
(41693, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'The Light be praised for your rescue. I thought I would\'ve ended like the rest of the corps. Thank you again, I\'ll tell you everything I know before getting out of this miserable place.', 0),
(41694, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'A pity, those were valuable agents we\'ve lost today. I\'ll send missives to their families, their service to the Kingdom won\'t be forgotten. Now, regarding this scroll...', 0),
(41695, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'I must say, it is thrilling to be on such a historical mission. The island of Balor is drenched in myths, legend and history. I can barely contain myself!$B$BOperative Gillian is a bit uneasy ever since we landed here, understandable, really. Not the most hospitable place. Still, we have a duty to fulfill, our service to the Alliance cannot be hindered by some measly ghosts. Either way, I take it you have something for me?', 0),
(41696, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'I see you are back, with writings in hand! Splendid, really. Having a few more phrases to compare and reference will make this whole ordeal all the more quicker. What I was able to find out is that their way of encoding their texts is very similar to historical documents we have from the Second War. Which leads me to believe that we are dealing with remnants and survivors of said war. Interesting, isn\'t it?$B$BRegardless, please let me finish the translation, it should not take too long, friend.', 0),
(41697, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Mission accomplished. Well done, $C. Sadly, I suspect we cannot ultimately cut off the demonic forces here with their warlocks still up and running. But we take any little victory we can get. Remember, this is a war against numbers, gotta use what you got to your advantage! Speaking of advantage, this tablet you brought with you has to contain crucial information about the demon\'s involvement in all of this. I just know it! I will bring it to Noppsy, he\'ll know what needs to be done.', 0),
(41698, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Ohoho, fine handiwork, friend. Those demon-hugging orcs will be in for a surprise once we press this detonator here and all the explosive goodness is just flying all around them!$B$B<Rufus\' eyes are full of glee, to the point where he appears like an overly joyous bearded child.>$B$BHo, this reminds me of that one time I almost blew up the Dwarven District in Stormwind. I\'ll share the story with you over an ale after we\'re done brooding over this blasted island. An honest dwarven promise!', 0),
(41699, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '<Verona is reading Noppsy\'s report without changing expressions. Her meticulous analysis of the report reminds you why she is the spearhead of this operation.>$B$B$N, ready yourself. We will launch an infiltration.', 0),
(41700, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'My compass! Does that mean Verix got what he deserved? Good riddance to him, if you ask me. One goblin\'s misery is another goblin\'s fortune, as we like to say. With my compass back in my possession, all that is left is to repair the Gullwing into workable shape. Thank you for your help, $C. You can keep some of the coins that Verix looted. If you want to keep lending your hand, we won\'t say no.', 0),
(41701, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Excellent work, $C. These fiends may be horrors beyond our comprehension, but at least they have a delicious taste to them. We can survive a few more days cooking a fine gumbo with it. Either way, it seems we are not done dealing with them just yet.', 0),
(41702, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'I have to admit, I\'m impressed. The others and I were waging with how many limbs you\'d return or if we\'d have to fish your limp body out of the ocean. Guess I\'ll owe Rikki some gold when we\'re back in Booty Bay. Regardless, incredible display of skills by you. Yunie will be relieved to have one less issue holding us back. If you\'re ever bored of adventuring around the world, the Steamwheedle Headquarters in Undermine are always in need of capable bruisers. Think about it, you\'d fit right in!', 0),
(41703, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Color me surprised, a whole treasure trove full of valuable materials. This alone should suffice for rebuilding the outer frame of the Gullwing. I have to say, I didn\'t expect you to be so successful. But that was to be expected for someone crazy enough to come to such a backwater island willingly, I suppose? Either way, we owe you one big time, friend. Goblin promise!', 0),
(41704, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Silence, not quite, but almost. My ghostly heart eases at your mercy. A noble deed of yours, truly. Had it not been for your kindness, the unrelenting torrent of their cries would have torn me into a vortex of insanity, that I am certain of. Balor\'s curse may be perpetual, yet its effects are now ever so slightly diminished. You are in my debt, $C.', 0),
(41705, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '<You place the fragmented doll in front of the woman\'s face and with a burst of unexpected ecstasy, her eyes widen as much as her brittle body allows it. With the last of her strength, she grasps the doll, with its edges digging deep into her hand, yet producing no blood flow. A last pitiful wailing is uttered before she stops moving entirely.$B$BWhether or not your last act made her death less painful, you can only guess. Atleast you can be certain that she is in agony no more.>', 0),
(41706, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'How vile... just being near them fills me with a burdening lethargy. This foulness is akin to what haunts our forests on Kalimdor, very much so. Yet still distinct enough to not be the same... I cannot fathom how painful it must\'ve been to live with such a shadow in one\'s body.', 0),
(41707, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '<Inspecting the mycelia under her monocle, Kinrial\'s face is masked in a stern expression; you assume both concern and critical intrigue.>$B$BInteresting, the mushroom strains continue seeking fertile ground to propagate in. Under normal circumstances they\'d quickly die if not nestled in fitting soil, but not these. They writhe and firm around, actively looking for nutrients. A harrowing sight. For our operatives\' sake, I will conceal this unsavory detail.', 0),
(41708, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'An unusally biting odor. Extracting a functioning poison from them might take some time, but the result will be worth the effort tenfold. I must thank you, your assistance accelerates the success of this mission more than you\'d think.', 0),
(41709, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'This shine and texture...! Even in this small chip of it, I can feel the tides resonate within it. And you picked it up from an enormous pearl on an altar, crackling with energy? I\'ll be honest with you, that sounds most alarming.', 0),
(41710, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'That old fool. He always had a knack for living on the edge, but he should really start caring more about his safety. Either way, I am glad he is still in good health. Now then, my book may be a bit waterlogged, but I can formulate the spell nevertheless.', 0),
(41711, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Naga, you say?! This is truly bad news. If these slithering demons are behind this phenomenon, then I dare not think what their true intentions are. For now we have thwarted their ambitions. However, I do wonder, has this pearl been here all along? If so, was it always broken? And if not, why was it brought here; and by whom? The naga or the murlocs? Many unanswered questions still lie before us and none of them seem to be easily answered. Either way, I must thank you for your assistance. Our findings today helped me gain a better understanding of Balor\'s unending storm. Once I return to Davenburg, I will send notice to the Council of Tides in Boralus about the pearl, as well as the naga\'s involvement in all of this. With their ongoing incursions onto Kul Tiras, I am afraid this won\'t be the last we\'ve seen of them.$B$BPlease, take this as humble compensation for your deeds.', 0),
(41760, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Frederik, old friend. Figments of your essence linger in this dull trinket, bare of any grandeur it once held. One day, when I may finally pass on and leave this realm, I will see you once more...$B$B$N, blessings upon you. This ring will find its way into oblivion, far away from the clutches of darkness, I will make sure of that. For your courageous act, take this from my remaining corporeal belongings. You deserve it well.', 0),
(41761, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'I expected nothing less. For an external aid, you\'ve proven yourself to be a valuable asset to our team. If the thrill of adventure ever subsides within you, the SI:7 has room for individuals like you.$B$BPlease, report your findings. Time is running out.', 0),
(41783, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '<Placing the books on Noppsy\'s table, the gnome marvels at the proportionally gigantic tomes.>$B$BSo beautiful and ancient! It will take some time to study these documents thoroughly. Thank you, $N. You\'ve done a great service to the kingdom today, preserving part of their history, as ugly and depressing as it may be. These stories tell us valuable lessons, so barring your eyes from them will only hurt you in the long run. Remember, knowledge is key to your survival.', 0),
(41786, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'It was a matter of time till someone dares to venture here. Lower your weapons, I mean you no harm.', 0),
(41787, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'What travesties have transpired at this place...? Never have I witnessed such horrors in my life, the thought of such profanities even existing send shivers down my spine.$B$B$N, your bravery in descending this spiral of madness is a heroic feat rarely seen nowadays. Your service to the kingdom and all of the Alliance this day will be remembered by those present and cherished by those affected. These rewards do not match the magnitude of your deeds, but take them nevertheless.$B$BYou are dismissed.', 0),
(41794, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Mok\'thardin did good in sending you here. This potion will prove to be vital in our endeavors on this island. While you are here, aid us. We could use any hand available.', 0),
(41795, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Whelpling, what we are facing is an abyss of unseen depth. Be absolutely sure your heart is steeled for what is to come. Lest you\'ll be devoured by the void festering on this island.', 0),
(41798, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Oh Ronald, your heart is in the right place, but your naivete is just too cumbersome sometimes. Either way, now that you\'re here, you might as well assist us. My name is Operative Verona Gillian, and I welcome you to the hell that is Balor.', 0),
(41799, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Hornby sent you? That fool is too soft for his own good. I appreciate the sentiment, but what is happening here exceeds whatever I was assigned to in Davenburg by far. Out of the question. He is right in one thing, however. Should you aid me in my research, I\'d be quicker to return to the mainland. So, what do you say?', 0),
(41813, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Magni\'s beard, an entire crate of it! So lucky this stuff doesn\'t go bad easily. Here you go, have some yourself.', 0),
(41814, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'While in poor condition, it is still the crown of a duke. This will prove those rascals in the Halls of Explorers wrong! Thank you, $R. Here is what I promised.', 0),
(41816, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'I smell blood in the air. You wear it like a second skin now. Good. Bring those tails here—we will feast on them.', 0),
(41817, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Your fear did not win today. Your eyes have changed, they look calmer now.', 0),
(41818, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'I am proud of the hunter you have become. Choose something of mine to carry as a memento of your success.', 0),
(41819, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'The irony of this scroll is lost on me.', 0),
(41820, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'O\'jin is on the right path; he has done well to send you instead of coming himself. A chieftain must know how to make the proper choice. This is valuable information, and for your trouble, a reward is due. There may come a time when I will seek your aid in dealing with this issue. I will return to my duties and soon speak with the Warchief. Beware of the shadows, $N, especially where they dance freely.', 0),
(41821, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'I will light a torch and perform a ritual to guide their souls to the afterlife. Thank you for setting them free.', 0),
(41822, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'A mercy far too great for scum like them. Take these; they will carry the light of An\'she with you through grim lands.', 0),
(41823, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'You have my thanks—and with them, a reward.', 0),
(41824, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'You have brought me its core? Well done. I will attempt to purify it now.', 0),
(41825, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Uda\'pe was right to send you to me. Though we are not very fond of working with the Horde, you have my thanks and will be paid accordingly.$B$BI will even add a bonus for being so silent and respectful—Uda\'pe taught you well.', 0),
(41826, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Mindless undead. Some are nothing more than flesh waiting to be cut down; others, the lingering essences of those who were—forever trapped. You have fulfilled your task.', 0),
(41827, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Mok\'gun\'s fate was sealed by Gul\'dan. He was not the first nor the last. Rest easy, stranger. This old wanderer has no quarrel with you or your kin. I am Drak\'thul, once a powerful warlock of the Stormreaver Clan. Now I am here to make sure I am the last of my kind.', 0),
(41828, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Stand proud child of the Horde. Victory is honorably achieved by those with strength and thunder in their blood.', 0),
(41829, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Good. Now I shall burn these wretched eyes, so the last thing their souls gaze upon is the fiery pits of the afterlife they deserve.', 0),
(41830, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'I see the color of blood and smell the stench of death on you. Well done. Now, onto other matters.', 0),
(41831, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Today, you have been the consequence of others. One day, your own will find you.', 0),
(41832, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'You know victory like no other—I\'m half a mind to challenge you myself.', 0),
(41833, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Well, what do you know... a ray of sunshine breaks through.', 0),
(41834, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Though it is not bound to be the last time we see the embers of the Shadow Council, a great victory was won. While we wish nothing from the land of Balor, it has given me the greatest gift.$B$BKilrogg was spiteful in the beginning, jealous of Grommash\'s celebration as a hero—while he himself seemed forgotten. But he was wrong to envy Grommash. My older brother merely set the foundation. It is you, and I, and Kilrogg who will build our future. I am glad he sees it that way now.', 0),
(41835, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'A step closer to the true goal.', 0),
(41836, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '<Drak\'thul cracks the box open.>$B$BWhat is this...?', 0),
(41837, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Both fragments together will now serve as the key to enter the ruins of the castle. Beware, for you will face both servants of the Legion and cultists of those long forgotten.', 0),
(41842, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Oh, more dusty than my grandmother back in Ironforge. Time has not been kind to this old tome, and the humid air is not exactly helping either. I will seal it properly in my chest and begin analysis back in the SI:7 headquarters. For you, $N, my heartfelt gratitude. Please choose a reward fitting for your service.', 0),
(41843, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Most impressive. It’s a shame you\'re not cut out for this field of work. Don’t get me wrong, you possess the skills and wits necessary, but I know your adventurous spirit cannot be tamed and seeks the grandeur of Azeroth. Still, the SI:7 owes you much, so let me reward you appropriately for all you’ve done.', 0),
(41844, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Wow, what a haul. Might not be exactly what we were supposed to be delivering, but I doubt those greedy bastards in their pirate cove will complain that much. Thank you so much, $N. We owe you big time. You can have this for your troubles, it always gave me the best of luck - the fact I’m still here is proof of that.', 0);
INSERT INTO `quest_request_items` (`ID`, `EmoteOnComplete`, `EmoteOnIncomplete`, `CompletionText`, `VerifiedBuild`) VALUES
(41692, 0, 0, '<Your surroundings suggest a fierce battle has taken place here, the carrion birds lurking around the ruined camp paint a grim picture. The journal you find among the scattered supplies may hold a clue on what happened here.>', 0),
(41693, 0, 0, 'Oh, what a relief to see another $R! Please, you have to get me out of here! Their leader is on the top floors, a burly one, with an iron fist! She has the key; quickly, we don\'t have much time!', 0),
(41694, 0, 0, '$N, you\'ve returned? Agent Deryl arrived here not long before you, his body strewn with grievous wounds. We\'ve sent him back to Stormwind for recuperation. But tell me, is there anything you could find?', 0),
(41695, 0, 0, 'Hello, friend; how may I help you?', 0),
(41696, 0, 0, 'Gel\'ror? No, no, no... Galbor? No, that\'s not it, either...', 0),
(41697, 0, 0, 'It is important to neutralize any threats before they can realize their full potential. Being two steps ahead of your enemy is a doctrine engrained in every SI:7 member.', 0),
(41698, 0, 0, 'Too bad I won\'t be able to see those beautiful explosions through all of this fog. I guess their sound will have to suffice for now.', 0),
(41699, 0, 0, 'Has Noppsy finished his translation? What have you found out?', 0),
(41700, 0, 0, 'Verix\' greed cost me my beautiful zeppelin, he has to answer for his crimes!', 0),
(41701, 0, 0, 'Drench the seas red with their icky blood, but keep a watchful eye out for the roaming sharks around here.', 0),
(41702, 0, 0, 'The way they\'re behaving makes you think there\'d be something for them here, but for the love of me, I cannot fathom just what it may be.', 0),
(41703, 0, 0, 'We can\'t spare too much time on the repairs, this humidity is not to be underestimated. I\'d prefer if the zeppelins hull would not break halfway through Stranglethorn, so hurry up, yes?', 0),
(41704, 0, 0, 'Their wailing haunts my undeath, a cacophony lamenting my incompetence as their lord.', 0),
(41705, 0, 0, '<Faint whimpering escapes her mouth.>', 0),
(41706, 0, 0, 'Shan\'do Staghelm possesses the knowledge to uncover this mystery. It is our duty to help him prevent this darkness from spreading.', 0),
(41707, 0, 0, '<Kinrial doesn\'t really pay attention to you.>', 0),
(41708, 0, 0, 'You may think a medic indulging in poison distillation is uncommon, but this is a required expertise in the SI:7, regardless of designation. My knowledge over the body and anatomy in particular gives me certain insights others may lack.', 0),
(41709, 0, 0, 'Kul Tiras and Balor share a history, were it not their ships to make trade with our fledgling nation many decades ago. As such I feel a distant connection and familiarity with this place, as faint as it may be.', 0),
(41710, 0, 0, 'From what we gathered I would assume the murlocs are collecting the shards of the broken pearl to complete it again. They do possess a degree of intelligence, more than enough to cast spells, yet even this is abnormal for what you\'d expect from your regular murloc.', 0),
(41711, 0, 0, 'All of this is more than puzzling, yet the situation calls for action, not speculation.', 0),
(41760, 0, 0, 'The history of Balor continues to be written, where it will lead, I do not know. But this chapter of its past needs to be closed, that I am certain of.', 0),
(41761, 0, 0, 'Do not venture alone. These beasts are unpredictable and will stop at nothing.', 0),
(41783, 0, 0, 'Balor was a place of hardship, tribulations and tragedies. Born from the wish for independancy and wealth, it quickly became the haven for merchants across the kingdom, and even those beyond its borders.', 0),
(41787, 0, 0, 'It may be too much to ask from you, but we don\'t have any luxuries left at this point.', 0),
(41794, 0, 0, 'Thrall hall, youngling. What brings you to Stormbreaker Point?', 0),
(41798, 0, 0, 'Ronald Gillian asked you to join his wife on Balor to assist in her work.', 0),
(41799, 0, 0, 'Speak with Hydromancer Finnigan in the SI:7 Outpost on Balor.', 0),
(41813, 0, 0, 'Hope it\'s worth the trouble, eh?', 0),
(41814, 0, 0, 'Did you come up with something?', 0),
(41816, 0, 0, 'Go out there and prove to yourself that you are the predator, not the prey.', 0),
(41817, 0, 0, 'Life is a battle, a battle against the aspects of your being that you cannot fully control.', 0),
(41818, 0, 0, 'Your final task awaits.', 0),
(41819, 0, 0, 'Slithering snakes, self acclaimed rulers of the seas and oceans—-a pain to deal with.', 0),
(41820, 0, 0, 'There is little time to spare. Speak.', 0),
(41821, 0, 0, 'It\'s so loud...', 0),
(41822, 0, 0, 'In time, An\'she will return to these lands.', 0),
(41823, 0, 0, 'This task can wait, but I would rather you fulfill it as quickly as possible.', 0),
(41824, 0, 0, 'The Earthmother will guide you to the answer.', 0),
(41825, 0, 0, 'Speak.', 0),
(41826, 0, 0, 'None are deserving of such a cruel fate.', 0),
(41827, 0, 0, 'Awful day for a swim.', 0),
(41828, 0, 0, 'Done yet?', 0),
(41829, 0, 0, 'I am prepared to set them aflame.', 0),
(41830, 0, 0, 'We owe apologies to none. It is not guilt that brought us here—but honor.', 0),
(41831, 0, 0, 'How thin the line between arrogance and confidence can be.', 0),
(41832, 0, 0, 'The queens of the colony are close. Keep a level head and push forward.', 0),
(41833, 0, 0, 'Ashes to ashes, dust to dust and scum to scum.', 0),
(41834, 0, 0, 'Lok\'tar ogar.', 0),
(41835, 0, 0, 'Legion or not, do what must be done.', 0),
(41836, 0, 0, 'I wonder what sort of dark, twisted artefact she holds that can provide her ownership of a copy of the key.', 0),
(41837, 0, 0, 'The lockbox merely contained the first fragment.', 0),
(41842, 0, 0, 'Stormwind always envied the Balorians on perfecting the art of successful trade not only with them, but several other nations as well. It’d be a shame if that knowledge would be lost in time, no?', 0),
(41843, 0, 0, 'I am sure you will run into more than enough fitting candidates for my task there.', 0),
(41844, 0, 0, 'You’re tough - or foolish - enough to come to this cursed place on your own, so I’m sure you’ll have no problems going in there and coming back out unharmed - mostly, atleast.', 0);
